        "original_id": "8fc85194-5cd9-5bdd-bb40-0bf142d03771",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Igor Dmitriev, Anastasiya Vertinskaya, Grigori Kozintsev, Yan Frid, Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov, Hamlet, Rosencrantz, Guildenstern, King Claudius\n- Works: Hamlet, The Green Carriage, Scarlet Sails, Amphibian Man\n- Roles: Rosencrantz\n- Topics: Russian and Soviet film and theater\n\nFacts:\n- Igor Borisovich Dmitriev (May 29, 1927 – January 26, 2008) was a Russian film and theater actor who specialized in aristocratic characters in costume productions.\n- In Grigori Kozintsev's Hamlet, Igor Dmitriev played Rosencrantz.\n- Rosencrantz and Guildenstern are childhood friends of Hamlet who are summoned by King Claudius to distract Hamlet from his apparent madness and, if possible, discover its cause.\n- The Green Carriage is a 1967 Soviet historical drama film directed by Yan Frid and starring Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov, and Igor Dmitriev.\n- Anastasiya Alexandrovna Vertinskaya, born on 19 December 1944 in Moscow, Soviet Union, is a Soviet and Russian actress.\n- Anastasiya Vertinskaya rose to prominence in the early 1960s through acclaimed performances in Scarlet Sails, Amphibian Man, and Grigori Kozintsev's Hamlet.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
